# DartDoc templates

Reuse shared docs with dartdoc templates. Reference implementation: `packages/atmos_binary_buffer`.

## Syntax

```dart
/// {@template atmos.area.topic.en}
/// Shared English text.
/// {@endtemplate}
///
/// {@template atmos.area.topic.ru}
/// Общий русский текст.
/// {@endtemplate}

/// {@macro atmos.area.topic.en}
///
/// Member-specific English line.
///
/// {@macro atmos.area.topic.ru}
///
/// Уникальная русская строка для этого члена.
void example() {}
```

- `{@template name}` … `{@endtemplate}` — define once
- `{@macro name}` — expand that block at the use site
- Edit the template body in one place; do not copy-paste the same paragraph onto every method

## Naming

`atmos.<area>.<topic>.<lang>`

| Part | Meaning | Examples |
|------|---------|----------|
| `area` | type / module | `binaryReader`, `bfloat16`, `binaryBuffer` |
| `topic` | reusable idea | `scalar`, `list`, `rounding`, `packInt` |
| `lang` | language | `en`, `ru` |

Large cross-cutting docs may omit `.en`/`.ru` and put both languages inside one template (see `atmos.binaryBuffer.packInt` in `lib/atmos_binary_buffer.dart`).

## Where to host templates

1. **Library / file docs** — templates in the top `library` or file comment (`bfloat16.dart`, `float16.dart`)
2. **Dummy const** — when templates are not library docs, attach them to an unused private const so dartdoc still sees them:

```dart
/// {@template atmos.binaryReader.scalar.en}
/// ...
/// {@endtemplate}
// ignore: unused_element
const Object? _binaryReaderScalarDocTemplate = null;
```

3. **Main library file** — long shared topics used by reader and writer (`packInt`)

## Bilingual member docs

Always **EN first, then RU**:

1. `{@macro …en}` (and any EN-only specifics / `###` headings)
2. blank `///` line
3. `{@macro …ru}` (and RU-only specifics)

Compose macros: a method may include several (`rounding` + `nan`). Only add unique lines that are not already in a template.

## When editing

- New similar API → reuse existing macros; add a new template only for a new shared idea
- Renaming a template id → update every `{@macro}` that references it
- Do not delete a template still referenced by macros
- Prefer `###` section headings inside templates when the block is a named topic (Rounding, NaN, …)
